1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,280
Hello everyone, and welcome to Two Cups English.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,720
I'm Mia, and Ben is here with me.

3
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,540
This podcast is for people who are learning English.

4
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:11,060
We speak slowly.

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,970
We use simple words.

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:16,400
And we repeat the important words many times.

7
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:20,070
Today, our topic is the evening.

8
00:00:20,071 --> 00:00:21,920
And how the evening shapes tomorrow.

9
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:25,370
Ben, what time did you go to bed last night?

10
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:27,480
Hi Mia.

11
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:28,960
Hi everyone.

12
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:32,439
Last night, I went to bed at eleven thirty.

13
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,880
Not bad.

14
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:39,200
But my phone was next to my pillow, and I looked at it for thirty minutes in the dark.

15
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,880
So, really, midnight.

16
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:44,980
And this morning was slow.

17
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:46,800
What about you, Mia?

18
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,020
How was your night?

19
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,120
Bad, Ben.

20
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,060
I went to bed at midnight.

21
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:53,860
My cup was on the desk.

22
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,840
My clothes were on the chair, on the floor, on the bed.

23
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,350
My phone was next to my pillow, full of light.

24
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:04,500
And this morning, I could not find my keys.

25
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:06,540
I could not find a clean shirt.

26
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:07,980
I was late.

27
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:11,940
No keys and no shirt, Mia.

28
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:14,460
That is a hard morning.

29
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,350
But let me ask a strange question.

30
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:18,400
Was it the morning's fault?

31
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:19,980
No, Ben.

32
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:22,100
That is the thing I understood today.

33
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:24,960
This morning did not start this morning.

34
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,640
It started last night.

35
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:29,720
The messy evening made the messy morning.

36
00:01:30,470 --> 00:01:33,100
And I think many people know this feeling.

37
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:35,270
The morning pays for the evening before.

38
00:01:36,350 --> 00:01:41,860
"The morning pays for the evening before." Mia, that is our topic today.

39
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:47,040
And it is good news, because the evening is easy to change.

40
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,120
So here is our plan.

41
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:53,580
In part one, we talk about our own evenings.

42
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:55,900
The bad ones and the good ones.

43
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,060
In part two, we ask why the evening shapes tomorrow.

44
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:03,720
And I have a true story for that.

45
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:08,880
In part three, we share five small things for tonight.

46
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:10,380
Does that sound good?

47
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:12,220
That sounds good, Ben.

48
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:16,520
And to everyone listening, please do not worry if you miss something.

49
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:17,880
You will hear it again.

50
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:24,640
You can listen while you cook dinner, while you wash the dishes, or while you get ready for bed.

51
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:25,240
Okay, Ben.

52
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,820
Part one.

53
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,100
Tell me about your evenings.

54
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:30,640
What were they like before?

55
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:33,480
Before, my evenings were too full, Mia.

56
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,760
I did not disappear.

57
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:37,260
I worked.

58
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,480
I answered emails at ten at night.

59
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:43,360
I planned tomorrow at eleven.

60
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:47,040
I "used" my evening, as I thought.

61
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:53,140
And then I lay in bed with a head full of tomorrow, and I did not sleep.

62
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:55,520
And yours?

63
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,420
Were they full, too?

64
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:58,740
The opposite, Ben.

65
00:02:59,329 --> 00:03:00,750
My evening was a hole.

66
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:04,019
Work ended, and I fell into the hole.

67
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:04,520
Sofa.

68
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:05,440
Phone.

69
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:06,400
Snacks.

70
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:07,329
Television.

71
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:10,300
Then it was midnight, and I was surprised.

72
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:12,360
Where did the evening go?

73
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:15,500
I did not rest, and I did not prepare.

74
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:17,970
I just disappeared for four hours.

75
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,180
So your evening was empty, Mia, and mine was too full.

76
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:24,680
And both of us were tired in the morning.

77
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:26,660
That is interesting.

78
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:28,990
The problem is not doing nothing.

79
00:03:29,510 --> 00:03:30,750
And it is not doing a lot.

80
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:33,480
The problem is doing the wrong things at night.

81
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:37,340
"The wrong things at night." Yes, Ben.

82
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:39,220
So what are the right things?

83
00:03:40,130 --> 00:03:42,359
Let me tell you what changed for me.

84
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:44,560
It was a small thing, again.

85
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:47,500
One evening, I was tired of losing my keys.

86
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:50,700
So before bed, I put the keys in a bowl by the door.

87
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:51,780
That is all.

88
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:53,120
Ten seconds.

89
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:55,680
A bowl by the door, Mia.

90
00:03:56,380 --> 00:03:57,459
Ten seconds at night.

91
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:58,620
And in the morning?

92
00:03:59,200 --> 00:03:59,920
Were the keys there?

93
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,280
They were there, Ben.

94
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,380
No searching.

95
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,380
No stress.

96
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:08,820
And I thought, "What else can I put in its place tonight?" The cup.

97
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:09,880
The clothes.

98
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:10,720
The bag.

99
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:13,920
Five small things, five minutes.

100
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:15,940
And the morning was different.

101
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:17,240
Not perfect.

102
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,160
Different.

103
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:19,260
Easier.

104
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,160
Not perfect.

105
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,060
Easier.

106
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:24,200
That is the right goal, Mia.

107
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,820
So what are your five small things now?

108
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:29,300
How do you get ready for tomorrow?

109
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,310
Tell us the whole evening.

110
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:32,360
Okay, Ben.

111
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:35,520
First, when I come home, the bag goes on the hook.

112
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:36,840
Not on the floor.

113
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:37,700
The hook.

114
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,980
Second, I put tomorrow's clothes on the chair.

115
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,460
One shirt, one pair of trousers.

116
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:47,920
Third, the cup goes in the sink, washed, and back on the shelf.

117
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:51,500
Fourth, the phone goes on the table in the kitchen.

118
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:52,840
Not in the bedroom.

119
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:56,060
Fifth, I write one line for tomorrow.

120
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,080
Just one.

121
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:58,860
That is my evening.

122
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:00,040
Ten minutes.

123
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:01,960
Ten minutes, Mia.

124
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:07,379
And I want to say something about the clothes, because it sounds small, and it is not.

125
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:11,900
When I choose tomorrow's shirt tonight, I make a decision when I have energy.

126
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:15,440
In the morning, I have no energy for decisions.

127
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:16,760
Which shirt?

128
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:17,920
Which shoes?

129
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,140
Breakfast or not?

130
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:23,680
By eight o'clock, I have spent all my energy on small choices.

131
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:29,660
"Small choices at night, big work in the morning." I like that, Ben.

132
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:33,000
And I think the phone is the biggest small choice.

133
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:36,120
My phone lived next to my pillow for years.

134
00:05:36,529 --> 00:05:38,300
The last thing I saw at night.

135
00:05:38,330 --> 00:05:40,140
The first thing I saw in the morning.

136
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,800
Where does your phone sleep now?

137
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,600
Still in the bedroom, Mia.

138
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:47,040
I know.

139
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:48,680
I know it is a problem.

140
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:51,140
My phone is my alarm, that is my excuse.

141
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:52,800
Where does yours sleep?

142
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:54,880
In the kitchen, Ben.

143
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:58,180
And the first thing I see in the morning is the window.

144
00:05:58,220 --> 00:05:58,760
The light.

145
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,100
The room.

146
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,800
It is quiet.

147
00:06:01,830 --> 00:06:05,240
That one change did more for my mornings than anything else.

148
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:07,840
Buy a small alarm clock, Ben.

149
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,000
Five dollars.

150
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,460
Then the phone can sleep in the kitchen too.

151
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:14,300
And tomorrow morning, you wake up ready.

152
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,040
Five dollars, Mia.

153
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:17,740
Okay.

154
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:19,680
That is my task for tonight.

155
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,970
Can I tell you about my worst evening?

156
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,570
Because it shows the other side.

157
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,080
Please, Ben.

158
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,680
Your worst evening.

159
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:30,059
I think everyone has one of those, and nobody talks about it.

160
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:31,340
What happened?

161
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:35,360
Last month, I had a big day coming, Mia.

162
00:06:35,390 --> 00:06:36,180
A presentation.

163
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:37,560
I was nervous.

164
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:39,280
So at night, I worked on it.

165
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:40,600
Until midnight.

166
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,000
Then one o'clock.

167
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:45,380
I changed one word, then changed it back.

168
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:47,440
I was not making it better.

169
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:51,600
I was just afraid, and working was a way to hold the fear.

170
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:54,940
Working as a way to hold the fear.

171
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:57,380
Ben, I know that night.

172
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:58,740
And in the morning?

173
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,460
In the morning, I was tired, Mia.

174
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,820
And the presentation was not better.

175
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:06,820
It was the same, and I was worse.

176
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:08,840
So now I have a rule.

177
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:12,160
The night before a big day, I stop at eight.

178
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:15,440
Whatever the work is, at eight, I close it.

179
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:17,740
You stop at eight, Ben?

180
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:19,680
Even when you are nervous?

181
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,970
Even when the work is not finished?

182
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:24,080
That sounds very hard.

183
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:27,460
Especially when I am nervous, Mia.

184
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:29,060
At eight, I close the work.

185
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:31,740
I do my small evening things.

186
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,320
Then something quiet.

187
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:33,800
A book.

188
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:34,840
Tea.

189
00:07:35,550 --> 00:07:36,600
And I go to bed at ten.

190
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:40,380
And the strange thing is, the presentation is better.

191
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:42,540
Not because I worked more.

192
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,080
Because I slept.

193
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:51,160
A rested head at nine in the morning is better than a tired head that worked until one.

194
00:07:51,190 --> 00:07:57,930
"A rested head is better than a tired head that worked more." Ben, I did not believe that for years.

195
00:07:58,420 --> 00:07:59,160
Now I know it.

196
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:02,340
Okay, so that was part one.

197
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:03,080
Our evenings.

198
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:10,540
A hole, a too-full night, a bowl by the door, five small things, and a rule to stop at eight.

199
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:13,359
Now, part two.

200
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:15,400
Why does the evening shape tomorrow?

201
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:20,440
Ben, you have a true story, and it is a very old one.

202
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:22,260
Very old, Mia.

203
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:24,160
Okay, part two.

204
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:26,060
This is a true story.

205
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:28,160
It is about Benjamin Franklin.

206
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:31,160
He lived in America in the seventeen hundreds.

207
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:35,380
He was a writer, a scientist, and a very busy man.

208
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:40,120
And in his autobiography, he shows his daily plan.

209
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:40,880
One page.

210
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:42,830
Every hour of the day.

211
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:45,260
Every hour, Ben?

212
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:48,800
One page for the whole day, from morning to night?

213
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,520
What did the page say?

214
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:55,480
In the morning, at five o'clock, he asked himself one question, Mia.

215
00:08:56,430 --> 00:09:02,920
"What good shall I do this day?" And in the evening, at six o'clock, he wrote something very simple.

216
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:05,440
"Put things in their places."

217
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:10,789
"Put things in their places." Ben, that is my bowl.

218
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:13,960
Two hundred years before my bowl.

219
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:17,700
Two hundred and fifty years, actually, Mia.

220
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:21,540
And at nine o'clock at night, he asked a second question.

221
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:25,920
"What good have I done today?" Then he slept.

222
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:28,820
So Franklin had three evening things.

223
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:30,740
Put things in their places.

224
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:33,210
Ask what went well.

225
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:33,440
Sleep.

226
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:35,460
Three things, Ben.

227
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:40,680
That is the whole evening plan of one of the busiest people in history.

228
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,680
Not a long list.

229
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,079
Not a big system.

230
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:44,450
Three things.

231
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:46,930
Why do you think he kept it so small?

232
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:50,420
I think he knew what we are learning today, Mia.

233
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:55,200
The morning question, "What good shall I do?", only works if the evening is ready.

234
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,060
A messy evening gives a messy morning.

235
00:09:58,760 --> 00:09:59,500
Even to Franklin.

236
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,039
And I think there is a second reason.

237
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,760
The evening has a strange kind of time.

238
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,360
A strange kind of time, Ben?

239
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:09,420
Time is time, I think.

240
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:12,000
An hour at night is an hour in the morning.

241
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:12,960
What do you mean?

242
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,960
In the morning, time is fast, Mia.

243
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:17,590
Everything is urgent.

244
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:21,400
In the evening, time is slow and soft.

245
00:10:21,430 --> 00:10:22,520
There is no bus to catch.

246
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:26,540
So the evening is the right time for small things.

247
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,860
Washing a cup at seven in the morning is stress.

248
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:32,200
Washing a cup at nine at night is almost nice.

249
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:34,540
Same cup, same water.

250
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:35,880
Different time.

251
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:40,860
"The evening is where small things are cheap." Yes, Ben.

252
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:44,100
And the morning is where the same things are expensive.

253
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,680
Can I ask about the word "ready"?

254
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:49,040
Because I think we misunderstand it.

255
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:51,360
How do we misunderstand it, Mia?

256
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:52,760
Ready is ready.

257
00:10:53,430 --> 00:10:57,440
The bag is packed, the shirt is clean, you are ready.

258
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:57,840
Or not?

259
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:01,560
We think ready is a feeling, Ben.

260
00:11:01,570 --> 00:11:07,239
"I feel ready for tomorrow." I spent years trying to feel ready at night, and I never did.

261
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:10,080
I lay in bed and thought, "Am I ready?

262
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:13,960
Am I ready?" And the answer was always no.

263
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,720
Because ready is not a feeling, Mia.

264
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:18,660
Ready is a state of things.

265
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:20,780
The bag is ready.

266
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,740
The shirt is ready.

267
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:23,520
The line is ready.

268
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,540
Things can be ready.

269
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:29,720
And when the things are ready, the feeling comes by itself.

270
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:33,600
Or it does not, and it does not matter.

271
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:34,820
The house is ready for you.

272
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:39,670
"The house is ready for me." Ben, I love that.

273
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:42,400
Now I do not ask if I feel ready.

274
00:11:42,849 --> 00:11:43,700
I look at the chair.

275
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:45,120
The shirt is there.

276
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:47,140
I look at the table.

277
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,180
The line is there.

278
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:52,220
Ready is on the chair and on the table, not in my head.

279
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,240
And my head can sleep.

280
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,700
And your head can sleep, Mia.

281
00:11:57,540 --> 00:12:00,020
That is the last reason the evening shapes tomorrow.

282
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:02,910
Sleep is the last thing the evening does.

283
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:08,990
A good evening makes a good sleep, the way a good morning makes a good day.

284
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:11,560
Can I add Franklin's second question here?

285
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:12,980
Because it changed my nights.

286
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:17,080
"What good have I done today?" That one, Ben?

287
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:19,640
I thought it was just a nice old sentence.

288
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,530
Does it really change something?

289
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:23,020
It does, Mia.

290
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:31,080
At night, I ask, "What went well today?" Not "What did I miss?" Not "What is left?" What went well.

291
00:12:31,180 --> 00:12:31,699
One thing.

292
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:32,860
Maybe two.

293
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:34,740
I said hello to a neighbor.

294
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:36,360
I finished the page.

295
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:38,020
I made a good soup.

296
00:12:38,780 --> 00:12:39,560
And then I sleep.

297
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,580
It sounds small.

298
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,420
But I sleep differently after that question.

299
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:47,040
Ben, my old question was the opposite.

300
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:51,100
At night, I made a list of everything I did not do.

301
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:53,140
A long list, in the dark.

302
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:56,280
And then I wondered why I could not sleep.

303
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:59,610
Franklin's question turns the head to the good things.

304
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,780
And the good things are quiet.

305
00:13:02,590 --> 00:13:04,380
The missing things are loud.

306
00:13:05,050 --> 00:13:06,640
"The good things are quiet.

307
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:12,100
The missing things are loud." Mia, that is the sentence for the wall tonight.

308
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,660
Okay, so that was part two.

309
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,720
Why the evening shapes tomorrow.

310
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:19,640
We talked about Franklin's three evening things.

311
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:23,160
We said the evening is where small things are cheap.

312
00:13:23,860 --> 00:13:27,300
And we said ready is a state of things, not a feeling.

313
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,540
Now, part three.

314
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:31,560
Five small things for tonight.

315
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,780
Mia, you go first.

316
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,660
Okay, part three.

317
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,960
My first thing is Franklin's rule.

318
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:39,140
Put things in their places.

319
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:40,700
Keys in the bowl.

320
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,260
Bag on the hook.

321
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:44,020
Cup on the shelf.

322
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,220
Each one is ten seconds.

323
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,660
Each one is nothing.

324
00:13:48,380 --> 00:13:52,279
But each one is also a small trap that the morning would fall into.

325
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:56,690
So the evening removes the traps before the morning walks in.

326
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:58,640
And the house is ready.

327
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:01,760
Removing the traps before the morning walks in, Mia.

328
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:02,440
I like that.

329
00:14:03,390 --> 00:14:04,730
My first thing is shoes.

330
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:07,320
It took me years to find it.

331
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:08,850
My shoes were always somewhere.

332
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:10,580
Under the sofa.

333
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,840
Behind the door.

334
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:12,600
One in the kitchen.

335
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:17,240
Every morning, thirty seconds of looking, and a small bad feeling.

336
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:20,960
Now, at night, the shoes go by the door.

337
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:21,540
Both of them.

338
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:22,830
Next to each other.

339
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,170
Five seconds.

340
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,580
Both shoes, next to each other, Ben.

341
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,340
Small is exact.

342
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,520
My second thing is tomorrow's clothes on the chair.

343
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:35,060
One shirt, one pair of trousers.

344
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:37,140
And I iron the shirt.

345
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:37,789
Only one.

346
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,440
While I iron, I think about nothing.

347
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,720
The iron goes back and forward.

348
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:47,900
And when the shirt is on the chair, the first hour of tomorrow is already made.

349
00:14:47,910 --> 00:14:54,020
"The first hour of tomorrow is on the chair." Mia, my second thing is for the hole after dinner.

350
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:57,120
The dishes are done, and there are two hours.

351
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,780
And the hole wants the phone.

352
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:01,640
So I have a small rule.

353
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,880
One thing with my hands.

354
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,340
I fix a drawer.

355
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:05,800
I water the plants.

356
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:07,060
I write a card.

357
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:08,860
Twenty minutes with hands.

358
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:11,750
And after that, the phone is less loud.

359
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,220
Something with hands, Ben.

360
00:15:14,610 --> 00:15:15,760
My ironing is that.

361
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:18,749
And my third thing is the one line.

362
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:22,300
Every evening, I write one line on a small paper.

363
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:23,970
Tomorrow's first thing.

364
00:15:24,570 --> 00:15:28,980
"Call the dentist." "Walk before work." One line.

365
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:31,680
I put it on the kitchen table, next to the phone.

366
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:33,760
So in the morning, I do not think.

367
00:15:34,250 --> 00:15:35,740
The paper already knows.

368
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:37,500
The evening decided.

369
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,840
The morning only does.

370
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:42,320
"The evening decided.

371
00:15:42,850 --> 00:15:47,880
The morning only does." Mia, my third thing is Franklin's question.

372
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:49,640
What went well today?

373
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:52,200
Say it out loud, or in your head.

374
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:53,320
One thing.

375
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:56,760
And my fourth thing is an end time.

376
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:58,020
Ten thirty.

377
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:00,080
Not because I am a child.

378
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:03,640
Because after ten thirty, nothing good happens.

379
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:05,140
No good work.

380
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:06,640
No good thinking.

381
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:09,100
Only the phone, and worry.

382
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:16,100
"After ten thirty, nothing good happens." Ben, that is true in my house too.

383
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:18,190
Can I ask you something?

384
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:21,560
What do you do when the evening goes wrong?

385
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:27,240
When you come home late, or tired, or sad, and the five things do not happen?

386
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:29,240
That happens, Mia.

387
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:31,460
Maybe one night in five.

388
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:34,900
I come home at eleven, and I have nothing left.

389
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:37,020
So I do one thing.

390
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:38,360
Not five.

391
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:39,420
One.

392
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:42,180
Usually the one line for tomorrow.

393
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:43,800
Ten seconds.

394
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:49,360
"First thing: coffee, then the email to Sarah." And I sleep.

395
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:52,400
So the clothes are not on the chair.

396
00:16:52,790 --> 00:16:54,140
The cup is on the desk.

397
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:57,120
But the morning has a first line, Ben.

398
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:01,500
And a morning with a first line is a morning that starts.

399
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:03,580
Exactly, Mia.

400
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,180
The five things are the good version.

401
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:09,060
One thing is the enough version.

402
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:11,720
Tomorrow does not need five things.

403
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:13,420
Tomorrow needs one.

404
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:15,640
And enough is enough.

405
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:17,890
Do you have a fifth thing?

406
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:19,810
Something for the weekend, maybe?

407
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:21,680
Yes, Ben.

408
00:17:22,059 --> 00:17:22,999
Sunday evening.

409
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:26,680
Many people feel sad on Sunday evening.

410
00:17:26,690 --> 00:17:27,890
The weekend is ending.

411
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:30,000
Monday is coming.

412
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:31,300
I used to feel that, too.

413
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:35,030
Sunday at six, a small grey feeling.

414
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:38,610
Now I use Sunday evening to make Monday.

415
00:17:39,180 --> 00:17:40,060
Not the whole week.

416
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:41,180
Monday.

417
00:17:41,940 --> 00:17:43,380
I choose Monday's clothes.

418
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:45,600
I write Monday's one line.

419
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:47,860
I put Monday's bag by the door.

420
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:51,700
And the grey feeling gets smaller, Mia?

421
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:54,780
Because Monday is not a wall anymore?

422
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:55,920
Much smaller, Ben.

423
00:17:56,620 --> 00:18:00,000
Monday is a shirt on a chair and a line on a paper.

424
00:18:00,569 --> 00:18:02,120
That is all Monday is.

425
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,780
And for our listeners who are learning English?

426
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:07,260
Is the evening a good time for English?

427
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,340
The best time, Mia, and nobody uses it.

428
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,860
Many learners study late at night.

429
00:18:14,569 --> 00:18:16,349
They are tired, and they push.

430
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:18,060
One more page.

431
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:20,060
One more list of words.

432
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:22,300
And the words do not stay.

433
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:25,240
A tired head does not keep words.

434
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:26,540
It drops them.

435
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:28,760
So here is my idea.

436
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:34,460
Study early in the evening, for twenty minutes, when the head is still open.

437
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:36,080
Then stop.

438
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:37,300
Sleep.

439
00:18:38,260 --> 00:18:39,080
And the words stay.

440
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:45,120
"The night does the work, not you." Ben, that is beautiful.

441
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:48,200
And this podcast is an evening thing, actually.

442
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,260
Put it on while you wash the cup.

443
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:53,580
Let the words go in while your hands are busy.

444
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:56,139
Tomorrow morning, the words are still there.

445
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,300
The night kept them.

446
00:18:58,940 --> 00:18:59,810
The night kept them.

447
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:06,380
And to everyone listening at night right now, thank you for choosing this for your evening.

448
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,280
You could be scrolling.

449
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:08,740
You are listening.

450
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:10,680
That is a small good thing.

451
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,940
Put it on Franklin's list tonight.

452
00:19:13,580 --> 00:19:14,540
"What went well today?

453
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:18,930
I listened to twenty minutes of slow English." That counts.

454
00:19:20,550 --> 00:19:21,480
That counts, Ben.

455
00:19:22,340 --> 00:19:24,880
And I think that is our message today.

456
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:27,280
The morning does not start in the morning.

457
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,380
It starts the night before.

458
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:31,700
A messy evening gives a messy morning.

459
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:35,000
A ready evening gives an easy morning.

460
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:41,860
And a ready evening is five small things, ten minutes, when time is cheap and soft.

461
00:19:41,870 --> 00:19:44,700
Tomorrow is on the chair.

462
00:19:44,779 --> 00:19:46,260
Tomorrow is on the chair.

463
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:52,710
Mia, let's repeat today's important words, slowly, because our listeners want to remember them.

464
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:54,390
Evening.

465
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:58,480
The end of the day, after work, before sleep.

466
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,220
A good evening.

467
00:20:00,990 --> 00:20:02,640
The evening shapes tomorrow.

468
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:05,200
Tomorrow.

469
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,320
The day after today.

470
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,180
Tomorrow's shirt.

471
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:09,920
Night.

472
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:12,300
When it is dark and we sleep.

473
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,080
Last night.

474
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:16,280
The night does the work.

475
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:18,980
Ready.

476
00:20:19,010 --> 00:20:19,580
Prepared.

477
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:21,460
A ready evening.

478
00:20:22,410 --> 00:20:23,420
The house is ready.

479
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:25,940
Small.

480
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:26,560
Not big.

481
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,680
Five small things.

482
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:30,960
Evening.

483
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:32,040
Tomorrow.

484
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:33,080
Night.

485
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:34,280
Ready.

486
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:35,580
Small.

487
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:38,100
Five words for tonight.

488
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:39,880
And one big idea.

489
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:41,900
Put things in their places.

490
00:20:42,740 --> 00:20:44,900
Now, Ben, do you have a question for our listeners?

491
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:46,900
Yes, Mia.

492
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:49,510
Everyone listening, here is my question.

493
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:52,180
What is your one evening thing?

494
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,120
The bowl for the keys?

495
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:55,680
The shirt on the chair?

496
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:57,650
The phone in the kitchen?

497
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:01,380
Write it in the comments in one short sentence.

498
00:21:02,100 --> 00:21:11,460
For example, "My evening thing is one line for tomorrow." Reading those sentences is our evening thing, actually.

499
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:14,160
We read them at night, with tea.

500
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:17,180
With tea, before the lights go off.

501
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:21,880
And if this episode helped you, please subscribe to Two Cups English.

502
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:24,680
We make a new episode every few days.

503
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:30,440
Slow English, simple words, and one true story each time.

504
00:21:30,470 --> 00:21:33,060
The full text of this episode is in the description.

505
00:21:33,780 --> 00:21:36,190
Read it tonight, or read it tomorrow.

506
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:39,180
Tomorrow is fine, this time.

507
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:40,220
It is on the chair.

508
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:44,500
Thank you for spending this evening with us.

509
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:46,880
Maybe you are washing the dishes.

510
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:48,160
Maybe you are in bed already.

511
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:52,680
Wherever you are, do one small thing before you sleep.

512
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:55,200
Put one thing in its place.

513
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:57,040
Write one line.

514
00:21:57,809 --> 00:21:58,680
And then rest.

515
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:01,619
Tomorrow is already a little bit made.

516
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:02,900
Good night.

517
00:22:04,820 --> 00:22:05,480
This is Mia.

518
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:07,040
And this is Ben.

519
00:22:07,959 --> 00:22:09,399
This was Two Cups English.

520
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:11,259
Put things in their places.

521
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:12,819
We will see you tomorrow.

